<title>SRI LANKA: WEATHER-LIGHT SHOWERS SEEN OVER PARTS OF S.LANKA.</title>
<headline>WEATHER-LIGHT SHOWERS SEEN OVER PARTS OF S.LANKA.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department forecast light showers at a few places in the central, Western, Sabaragamuwa provinces and the southern Galle district for Saturday.</p>
<p>It said isolated thundershowers are likely in the Uva and east during Saturday afternoon.</p>
<p>It released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Friday morning:</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Canyon		    3.4</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    19.7</p>
<p>    Kotmale		  22.5</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 32.0</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     15.3</p>
<p>    Norton		   26.9</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0.9</p>
<p>    Victoria		  2.5</p>
</text>
